{
    "about": "The lines of UDS Table 5 (Staffing and Utilization). A line with a category is a personnel line: visits counts its clinic (in-person) and virtual visits (Columns B and B2); false means the manual grays those columns out because the personnel aren't providers. A line with sum adds up other lines. patients names the service category whose unduplicated patients go in Column C; \"sum\" adds the categories' patients, as Line 34 does. FTEs (Column A) come from HR records and aren't computed.",
    "basis": "2026 UDS Manual (HRSA, revised 2026-08-10), Table 5 on pages 69-70 and its instructions on pages 50-64, including the countable visit rules on pages 17-21 and the FAQ on pages 65-68. PDF sha256 02761d82af5b4786. Column grays checked against the table's rendering on page 70.",
